WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:01.380
- I'm Robin.

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:03.170
- Pleasure to meet you.

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:04.003
Is he here?

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:05.624
- Is who here?

00:00:05.624 --> 00:00:07.120
(pirate music)

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.138
- Henderson.

00:00:08.138 --> 00:00:08.971
(laughing)

00:00:08.971 --> 00:00:09.825
Henderson.

00:00:09.825 --> 00:00:11.363
He's back, he's back.

00:00:11.363 --> 00:00:12.196
- I'm back.

00:00:12.196 --> 00:00:13.029
- You got the job!

00:00:13.029 --> 00:00:13.862
- I got the job!

00:00:13.862 --> 00:00:15.220
(laughing)
(mimicking trumpet)

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:17.187
(slower trumpet mimicking)

00:00:17.187 --> 00:00:18.829
Hey!

00:00:18.829 --> 00:00:22.262
(fake fighting)

00:00:22.262 --> 00:00:24.512
(laughing)

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.203
- How many children are you friends with?

00:00:29.203 --> 00:00:30.036
- [Judgemental Voice] Boom!

00:00:30.036 --> 00:00:32.740
And another one bites the dust.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:35.810
You are oh for six, Popeye.

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:37.240
- Yeah, yeah, I can count.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.790
- You know that means you suck.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:41.200
- Yup, I can read too.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.500
- Since when?

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.010
- It's the stupid hat.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.830
I am telling you, it is totally
blowing my best feature.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.417
- Yeah, company policy is a real drag.

00:00:49.417 --> 00:00:52.667
(slow saxophone music)

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.250
- Hey twelve o'clock.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.483
- Oh shit, oh shit, okay.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:01.443
Going in, okay, look.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:03.950
And you know what,

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:04.783
(crash)

00:01:04.783 --> 00:01:05.616
screw company policy.

00:01:05.616 --> 00:01:06.810
- Oh my god, you're a whole new man.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:07.643
- Right?

00:01:08.836 --> 00:01:10.003
- Well ladies,

00:01:11.372 --> 00:01:12.205
- Oh god.

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.320
- Can I get you guys a little
taste of Cherries Jubilee?

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.153
No?

00:01:15.153 --> 00:01:15.986
Anybody?

00:01:15.986 --> 00:01:16.819
Banana Boat?

00:01:16.819 --> 00:01:18.410
Four people, four spoons?

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:19.741
Share it in the booth?

00:01:19.741 --> 00:01:20.850
- [Judgemental Voice] You suck.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.241
- Do you have a quarter?

00:01:22.241 --> 00:01:23.599
- (chuckles)

00:01:23.599 --> 00:01:24.750
Are you sure you are tall
enough for that ride?

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:25.583
- Quarter!

00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:26.416
- Whoa!

00:01:26.416 --> 00:01:27.312
(quarter clinking)

00:01:27.312 --> 00:01:29.590
(carnival music)

00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:31.036
- Do you need help
getting up little Stevie?

00:01:31.036 --> 00:01:32.847
- Whoa! (laughs)

00:01:32.847 --> 00:01:33.680
- We're going down!

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:34.513
We're going down!
(elevator falling)

00:01:34.513 --> 00:01:36.198
- Yeah, no shit Harrington!

00:01:36.198 --> 00:01:37.800
- (screeching)

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.063
- Look away! (sighs)

00:01:41.325 --> 00:01:44.242
(electronic music)

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.996
- Can you redirect your stream please?

00:01:48.996 --> 00:01:50.780
(percussive sting)

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:54.650
I hate to break it to you,
but this is not water.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:56.200
- No, but it's a liquid

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.320
and if it comes down to
me drinking that shit

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.671
or dying of thirst, I drink.

00:02:00.671 --> 00:02:03.421
(glass breaking)

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.250
- Jesus Christ
- Ooh

00:02:09.902 --> 00:02:10.759
Do you still want to drink that?

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:11.914
(screeching)

00:02:11.914 --> 00:02:15.100
- I don't know, but it's possible.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:15.933
- I'm sorry, is there something you two

00:02:15.933 --> 00:02:17.373
would like to share with the class?

00:02:17.373 --> 00:02:19.110
(suspenseful beat)

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:19.943
(electronic music)

00:02:19.943 --> 00:02:20.900
- I could just take him out.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.290
- Take who out?

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.369
- The Russian guard.

00:02:23.369 --> 00:02:25.523
(upbeat music)

00:02:25.523 --> 00:02:27.810
- And, in the meantime, sling ice cream,

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:29.977
behave, and don't get beat up.

00:02:29.977 --> 00:02:32.960
(screaming)

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:35.710
- I'm gonna die in a secret Russian base

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:37.280
with Steve "the Hair" Harrington.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.302
(mimicking trumpet)

00:02:38.302 --> 00:02:39.590
- Hey!

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:40.423
Boop.

00:02:40.423 --> 00:02:42.540
- We all die my strange
little child friend.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:46.040
It's just a matter of how, and when.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.031
- [Confused Voice] Wha?

00:02:47.031 --> 00:02:48.390
(knife unsheathed)

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:49.940
- Would now be a good time

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.670
to tell you that I don't like doctors?

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:53.393
- Whoa! (laughs)

00:02:53.393 --> 00:02:58.393
- You broadcast that stupid
spy shit all over town

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:00.060
and we picked it up on our Cerebro

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.953
and we cracked it in a day!

00:03:02.787 --> 00:03:03.908
A day!

00:03:03.908 --> 00:03:04.747
(faint static)

00:03:04.747 --> 00:03:05.580
A day!

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:06.595
(static)

00:03:06.595 --> 00:03:07.428
A day!

00:03:07.428 --> 00:03:08.400
(intensified static)

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.690
You think you are so smart

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:14.715
but a couple of kids, who
scoop ice cream for a living,

00:03:14.715 --> 00:03:16.170
(electronic music)

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:19.400
cracked your code in a day and
now people know you are here.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.050
- Ooh, I just got the chills.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:23.925
From this float, not your speech.

00:03:23.925 --> 00:03:25.700
- (groaning in pain)

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.630
- I know his taste is a bit pedestrian

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:29.851
but dingus has other qualities.

00:03:29.851 --> 00:03:31.028
- (mimicking trumpet)

00:03:31.028 --> 00:03:33.429
(falling over)

00:03:33.429 --> 00:03:34.660
(upbeat music)

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:35.740
- I'm Robin

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:37.060
She sounds awesome.

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:38.125
- She is awesome.

00:03:38.125 --> 00:03:40.708
(heroic music)

